{{also|Rainbow}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:WhereRainbowRises.jpg|thumb|right|250px|A '''rainbow''' (multicoloured arch shape).]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰewgʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|reynbowe}}, {{m|enm|raynbowe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|reġnboga|t=rainbow}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*regnabogō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*regnabugô|t=rainbow}}, equivalent to {{com|en|rain|bow|t2=arch}}. Cognate with {{cog|fy|reinbôge|t=rainbow}}, {{cog|nl|regenboog|t=rainbow}}, {{cog|de|Regenbogen|t=rainbow}}, {{cog|da|regnbue|t=rainbow}}, {{cog|sv|regnbåge|t=rainbow}}, {{cog|is|regnbogi|t=rainbow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹeɪnboʊ/|/ˈɹeɪmboʊ/|a=GenAm}}; {{enPR|rān'bō|rām'bō}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹeɪnbəʊ/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-rainbow.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|arch in sky created by water droplets}} A [[multicoloured]] [[arch]] in the [[sky]], produced by [[prismatic]] [[refraction]] of [[light]] within [[droplet]]s of [[rain]] in the [[air]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1979|artist=Kermit the Frog (Jim Henson)|title=Rainbow Connection|author=Paul Williams; Kenneth Ascher|passage=Why are there so many songs about '''rainbows'''<br />And what's on the other side?<br />'''Rainbows''' are visions, but only illusions<br />And '''rainbows''' have nothing to hide.}}
# {{senseid|en|any spectrum of colors with similar appearance as rainbow in sky}} Any prismatic refraction of light showing a [[spectrum]] of [[colour]]s.
# {{lb|en|often used with “of”}} A [[wide]] [[assortment]]; a [[varied]] [[multitude]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''rainbow''' of possibilities}}
# {{senseid|en|illusion}} {{lb|en|figurative}} An [[illusion]]; a [[mirage]].
#: {{ux|en|Many electoral promises are '''rainbows''', vanishing soon after poll day.}}
# {{senseid|en|slow curveball or any curveball}} {{lb|en|baseball}} A [[curveball]], particularly a slow one.
# {{senseid|en|type of flop in card games}} {{lb|en|poker slang}} In [[Texas hold 'em]] or [[Omaha hold 'em]], a [[flop]] that contains three different [[suit]]s.
# {{cap|rainbow trout}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1911|author=Francis R. Steel|chapter=Catching the Rainbow Trout|title=The Outing Magazine|volume=58|page=482
|passage=Finally, by actual trial, I have found that I can catch more '''rainbow''' by using one fly than with a two or three-fly cast.}}
# {{senseid|en|an lgbt person}} {{lb|en|metaphorically|sometimes|derogatory}} A person within the [[LGBT]] community.
#: {{ux|en|Oh look, the '''rainbow''' came back.}}

